<resources>
    <!-- Title of the single refresh-rate control in Settings -> Display.

         Upstream calls this "Peak refresh rate" because upstream's control only
         ever writes PEAK_REFRESH_RATE. On this device it is the ONLY refresh
         rate control (config_show_min_refresh_rate_switch is false beside this
         file) and apply-overlays-v2 step 44 makes it write BOTH bounds, so
         picking "90Hz" LOCKS the panel at 90 rather than capping it. "Peak"
         would then be actively wrong, and "Smart" listed under a heading that
         says "Peak" reads as nonsense.

         🔑 THIS IS A PER-CONFIG OVERRIDE, NOT A GLOBAL ONE, and that is the
         whole reason it is safe. DEVICE_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS on this product is a
         STATIC overlay, not an RRO — PRODUCT_ENFORCE_RRO_TARGETS is unset, no
         auto-generated RRO for Settings exists in the build output, and
         package_internal.mk:154 therefore takes the static branch. aapt2 then
         merges overlay resources by (name, CONFIG) pair, so replacing the
         default-config entry leaves every other locale untouched.

         Proven with aapt2 before shipping, not assumed — a throwaway target
         with values/, values-in/ and values-fr/, overlaid by a values/ +
         values-in/ pair, linked with aapt2's auto-add-overlay flag:

             resource string/max_refresh_rate_title
               ()   "Refresh rate"                       <- ours
               (in) "Kecepatan refresh"                  <- ours
               (fr) "Taux de rafraichissement maximal"   <- UPSTREAM, SURVIVED

         ⚠ Stated honestly, because it is a real limitation: the ~30 locales
         upstream already translates keep their own wording, which still says
         "peak" or "maximum". That is imprecise for a locking control, but it is
         localized and not broken, and inventing translations for 30 languages
         is not something this project can verify. English and Indonesian — the
         two locales this ROM's users actually run — are correct. If a
         translation for another locale is ever contributed, it drops in here as
         one more values-<lang>/ file with no code change. -->
    <string name="max_refresh_rate_title">Refresh rate</string>
</resources>
